Replace it with this corrected version:

```javascript
            // Completed Activities
            const completed = maintenance.filter(m => m.status === 'completed');
            if (completed.length > 0) {
                maintY = checkAndAddPage(doc, maintY, 30);
                doc.setFontSize(12);
                doc.setFont(undefined, 'bold');
                doc.setTextColor(0, 0, 0);
                doc.text('Completed Activities', 20, maintY);
                maintY += 8;
                
                doc.setFontSize(9);
                doc.setFont(undefined, 'normal');
                doc.setTextColor(80, 80, 80);
                doc.text(completed.length + ' maintenance task(s) completed', 25, maintY);
                maintY += 10;
                
                completed.slice(-5).reverse().forEach(function(item) {
                    maintY = checkAndAddPage(doc, maintY, 15);
                    
                    // Extract and clean the activity name
                    var activityName = item.activity || 'Unnamed';
                    // Remove all special characters and normalize spaces
                    activityName = activityName.replace(/[&<>]/g, '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
                    
                    doc.setFontSize(9);
                    doc.setTextColor(40, 167, 69);
                    // Use string concatenation instead of template literals to avoid encoding issues
                    doc.text('✓ ' + activityName.substring(0, 45), 30, maintY);
                    maintY += 5;
                    
                    doc.setFontSize(8);
                    doc.setTextColor(100, 100, 100);
                    var completedDate = formatDateStr(item.date);
                    doc.text('Completed: ' + completedDate, 32, maintY);
                    maintY += 8;
                });
            }
```

The key changes:

1. Removed template literals (backticks) - using simple string concatenation instead
2. Added specific character filtering - removing &, <, > symbols
3. Changed arrow function to regular function - avoids any scope-related encoding issues
4. Used var instead of let - more compatible with jsPDF's text rendering

If the issue persists, here's an even more aggressive fix that forces plain ASCII text:

```javascript
            // Completed Activities (ULTRA CLEAN VERSION)
            const completed = maintenance.filter(m => m.status === 'completed');
            if (completed.length > 0) {
                maintY = checkAndAddPage(doc, maintY, 30);
                doc.setFontSize(12);
                doc.setFont(undefined, 'bold');
                doc.setTextColor(0, 0, 0);
                doc.text('Completed Activities', 20, maintY);
                maintY += 8;
                
                doc.setFontSize(9);
                doc.setFont(undefined, 'normal');
                doc.setTextColor(80, 80, 80);
                doc.text(completed.length + ' maintenance task(s) completed', 25, maintY);
                maintY += 10;
                
                completed.slice(-5).reverse().forEach(function(item) {
                    maintY = checkAndAddPage(doc, maintY, 15);
                    
                    // Force plain ASCII - remove everything except letters, numbers, spaces, and basic punctuation
                    var activityName = item.activity || 'Unnamed';
                    activityName = activityName.replace(/[^a-zA-Z0-9\s\-\.]/g, '').replace(/\s+/g, ' ').trim();
                    
                    doc.setFontSize(9);
                    doc.setTextColor(40, 167, 69);
                    doc.text('✓ ' + activityName.substring(0, 45), 30, maintY);
                    maintY += 5;
                    
                    doc.setFontSize(8);
                    doc.setTextColor(100, 100, 100);
                    var completedDate = formatDateStr(item.date);
                    doc.text('Completed: ' + completedDate, 32, maintY);
                    maintY += 8;
                });
            }
```

This ultra-clean version only allows:

· Letters (a-z, A-Z)
· Numbers (0-9)
· Spaces
· Hyphens and periods

Everything else (including ampersands, quotes, special characters) gets stripped out.
